@{
    
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}

<style>
    body {
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    }

    .bg-welfare-left {
        background-color: #0747AE;
        padding: 15px;
    }

        .bg-welfare-left h3 {
            font-size: 21px;
            font-weight: 600;
            color: #fff;
        }

        .bg-welfare-left ul li {
            margin-top: 18px;
            font-size: 17px;
            color: #fff;
        }

            .bg-welfare-left ul li a {
                color: #fff;
                text-decoration: none;
            }

                .bg-welfare-left ul li a:hover {
                    text-decoration: underline;
                }

    .content-box {
        border: 1px dashed #000;
        background: #fff;
        padding: 20px;
        height: 100% !important;
    }

    .welfare-font {
        font-size: 17px;
        color: #000;
        text-align: justify;
        line-height: 1.8;
    }

    hr {
        border: 1px solid #000;
    }
</style>

<!-- ================= BANNER ================= -->
<div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-12 p-0" style="margin-top:-20px;
        background:url('https://img.freepik.com/premium-photo/extensive-collection-books-library_868797-8212.jpg') center/cover fixed;">
        <div style="background:rgba(0,0,0,0.5)">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="d-flex flex-column justify-content-center" style="min-height:300px;">
                    <h3 class="display-6 text-white fw-bold">
                        Department of Applied Sciences & Humanities (APSH)
                    </h3>
                    <div class="d-inline-flex text-white">
                        <a href="/" class="text-white text-decoration-none">Home</a>
                        <i class="fa fa-angle-double-right px-2 pt-1"></i>
                        <span>Department of Applied Sciences & Humanities (APSH)</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ================= MAIN CONTENT ================= -->
<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="row">
        <style>
            .bg-welfare-left ul li {
                margin-top: 20px;
                font-size: 19px;
                line-height: 1.5;
                color: #fff;
                font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            }

            .bg-welfare-left hr {
                border-bottom: 2px solid white !important;
            }
        </style>
        <!-- LEFT SIDEBAR -->
        <div class="col-lg-3">
            <div class="bg-welfare-left h-100">
                <h3 class="text-uppercase">Side Tabs</h3>
                <hr>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li> <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-up-right-from-square" style="font-size:16px;"></i> <a href="~/home/ASH_Vision">Vision</a></li>
                    <hr>
                    <li> <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-up-right-from-square" style="font-size:16px;"></i><a href="~/home/ASH_Mision"> Mission</a></li>
                    <hr>
                    <li> <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-up-right-from-square" style="font-size:16px;"></i> <a href="~/home/ASH_Faculty"> Faculty</a></li>
                    <hr>
                    <li> <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-up-right-from-square" style="font-size:16px;"></i><a href="~/home/ASH_Facilities"> Facilities</a></li>
                    <hr>

                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- RIGHT CONTENT -->
        <div class="col-lg-9">
            <div class="content-box">
                <h2 class="fw-bold mt-5" style="color:#0747AE;">Departmental Laboratories</h2>
                <hr>

                <div class="row g-4 mt-2">



                    <h5 class="fw-bold" style="font-size:18px;">Engineering Physics Laboratory</h5>
                    <p class="welfare-font" style="margin-top:-5px;">
                        The engineering physics laboratory at Bharat Ratna Babasaheb Bhimrao Ambedkar Rajkiya Engineering College Pratapgarh, offers outcome-based education across a broad spectrum of fundamental and applied physics. The laboratory is equipped with state-of-the-art facilities to support experiments in emergent interdisciplinary areas such as optics, mechanics, and magnetism. It prepares students for industrial competencies, advanced research, and higher studies, where strong grounding in physical and natural sciences is essential.
                    </p>

                    <p class="welfare-font" style="font-size:18px; margin-top:-12px;"><b>List of Experiments</b></p>
                    <ul class="welfare-font" style="margin-top:-17px; list-style-type:disc; margin-left:20px;">
                        <li>Newton's Rings</li>
                        <li>Plane diffraction grating</li>
                        <li>Nodal slide</li>
                        <li>Fresnel biprism</li>
                        <li>Energy band gap</li>
                        <li>Stefan's law</li>
                        <li>Variation of magnetic field</li>
                        <li>Carey Foster Bridge</li>
                        <li>Viscosity</li>
                        <li>Combination of two lenses</li>
                        <li>Attenuation in optical fiber</li>
                        <li>He-Ne laser light using single slit diffraction/polarization of light</li>
                        <li>Hall Effect</li>
                        <li>Hysteresis B-H curve</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h5 class="fw-bold mt-4" style="font-size: 18px;">Engineering Chemistry Laboratory</h5>
                    <p class="welfare-font" style="margin-top:-5px;">
                        The engineering chemistry laboratory of the department supports engineering students in their foundational and applied studies. It provides a safe working environment, high-quality chemicals, and modern instruments to facilitate hands-on experiments in engineering chemistry. Key equipment includes pH meters, conductometers, viscometers, digital weighing balances, and high-precision glassware, enabling students to develop practical skills, analytical thinking and experimental competence essential for engineering applications and research.
                    </p>

                    <p class="welfare-font" style="font-size: 18px;"><b>List of experiments</b></p>
                    <ul class="welfare-font" style="margin-top:-10px; list-style-type:disc; margin-left:20px;">
                        <li>Analytical and volumetric chemistry</li>
                        <li>Water hardness and water-quality analysis</li>
                        <li>Polymer chemistry and viscosity measurements</li>
                        <li>Polymer chemistry and viscosity measurements</li>
                        <li>Corrosion studies and electrochemical methods</li>
                        <li>Instrumental analysis and material characterization</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h5 class="fw-bold mt-4" style="font-size: 18px;">Language and Soft Skills Lab</h5>
                    <p class="welfare-font" style="margin-top:-5px;">
                        The language and soft skills laboratory is a modern technology enabled facility designed to enhance students communication abilities and professional competencies. It is equipped with the state-of-the-art All-in-One computers featuring in-built audio-visual tools and microphones, providing an interactive environment for improving pronunciation, fluency, and overall English proficiency. The lab supports activities that strengthen listening, speaking, reading, and writing skills, while fostering teamwork, leadership, critical thinking, and positive body language, preparing students for academic, professional, and interpersonal success.
                    </p>

                    <p class="welfare-font" style="font-size:18px;"><b>Key Activities</b></p>
                    <ul class="welfare-font" style="margin-top:-10px;"> 
                        <li>Pronunciation, accent-neutralization, and vocabulary-building sessions</li>
                        <li>Listening modules, spoken English practice, and grammar drills</li>
                        <li>Group discussions, debates, and presentation practices</li>
                        <li>Mock interviews, role-plays, and professional etiquette training</li>
                    </ul>

                    <p class="welfare-font mt-4">
                        Together, the laboratories of the Applied Sciences and Humanities Department (APSH) create a comprehensive learning environment that reinforces foundational knowledge in applied sciences while enhancing professional communication skills, thereby improving students’ confidence, communication proficiency and employability.
                    </p>


                </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
